---
import Adr from "../components/Adr.astro";
import Diagram from "../components/Diagram.astro";
import Excerpt from "../components/Excerpt.astro";
import Inferred from "../components/Inferred.astro";
import Layer from "../components/Layer.astro";
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";
import Path from "../components/Path.astro";
import Rule from "../components/Rule.astro";
import Sequence from "../components/Sequence.astro";

const APP = "web/app/src";
const ROUTER = "web/app/src/router.tsx";
const SDK = "web/packages/sdk/src/index.ts";
const FRAME = "web/app/src/component-frame.tsx";
const CV = "server/src/iki_server/components/views.py";

const boxes = [
  { id: "shell", x: 20, y: 30, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Django page shell", sub: "one template, no data" },
  { id: "build", x: 250, y: 30, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Vite build", sub: "/static/app/, immutable" },
  { id: "router", x: 480, y: 30, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Router", sub: "routes with loaders", strong: true },
  { id: "layout", x: 710, y: 30, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Layout", sub: "sidebar, palette" },
  { id: "query", x: 480, y: 150, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Query cache", sub: "page reads, 30 s stale" },
  { id: "sdk", x: 250, y: 150, w: 190, h: 60, label: "@ikisci/sdk", sub: "generated from OpenAPI" },
  { id: "api", x: 20, y: 150, w: 190, h: 60, label: "/api/v1 and events", sub: "session, CSRF, SSE" },
  { id: "ui", x: 710, y: 150, w: 190, h: 60, label: "@ikisci/ui", sub: "tokens, button, sidebar" },
  { id: "science", x: 710, y: 270, w: 190, h: 60, label: "@ikisci/science", sub: "viewers and inputs" },
  { id: "workers", x: 480, y: 270, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Workers and iki-wasm", sub: "rules, parsers, apps" },
  { id: "frames", x: 250, y: 270, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Plugin frames", sub: "sandboxed, by digest" },
  { id: "still", x: 20, y: 270, w: 190, h: 60, label: "Stability checks", sub: "lint rules, press tests" },
];
const edges = [
  { from: "shell", to: "build" },
  { from: "build", to: "router" },
  { from: "router", to: "layout" },
  { from: "router", to: "query", label: "loaders" },
  { from: "query", to: "sdk" },
  { from: "sdk", to: "api" },
  { from: "layout", to: "ui" },
  { from: "ui", to: "science", dashed: true },
  { from: "science", to: "workers" },
  {
    from: "router",
    to: "frames",
    label: "plugin tabs",
    via: [
      [460, 110],
      [460, 240],
      [345, 240],
    ] as [number, number][],
    at: [400, 232] as [number, number],
  },
  { from: "still", to: "frames", dashed: true },
];

const H = {
  short: "What the browser runs",
  how: "From a URL to a page that holds still",
  example: "A plasmid's map, drawn by its plugin in a frame",
  rules: "Routing, data, the SDK, packages, frames, stability and serving",
  ref: "Code and decisions",
};
const toc = [
  { id: "short", label: H.short },
  { id: "how", label: H.how },
  { id: "frame-seq", label: "A plugin tab, step by step" },
  { id: "example", label: H.example },
  { id: "rules", label: H.rules },
  { id: "ref", label: H.ref },
];
---

<Layout toc={toc}>
  <Layer n={1} title={H.short}>
    <p>
      The web app is a React app that Django serves as one template for every app path, with no
      data in it. TanStack Router's loaders read through TanStack Query, and every read goes through
      a TypeScript client generated from the server's OpenAPI document, so a server change that
      breaks a page fails a check. Scientific views come from <code>@ikisci/science</code>, the
      basic controls and tokens from <code>@ikisci/ui</code>, and plugins draw their own views in
      sandboxed frames the page talks to over a private port. Pages read what decides their buttons
      before they render, so nothing moves under a press, and the browser tests fail if it does.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>React pages served by Iki, beside server-rendered ones (<Adr n="0029" />).</li>
      <li>Plugin components run in sandboxed frames (<Adr n={[84, 102]} />).</li>
      <li>Web components are published by entry point (<Adr n="0191" />).</li>
      <li>The app is laid out around a sidebar, and what you can read (<Adr n="0176" />).</li>
    </ul>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={2} title={H.how}>
    <Diagram id="webapp" title="The web app's parts, from the page shell to plugin frames" width={920} height={350} boxes={boxes} edges={edges}>
      <div slot="shell">
        <p>
          Every app path is also a Django route serving <code>web/app.html</code>: sign-in required,
          the CSRF token in a meta tag, module preloads and the entry script. It answers 503 when the
          build is missing (<Adr n="0029" />).
        </p>
        <p><Path p="server/src/iki_server/web/views.py" sym="def app(" />, <Path p="server/src/iki_server/web/templates/web/app.html" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="build">
        <p>
          Vite builds into Django's static files; hashed files are cached for good. In development a
          header switches the shell to Vite's modules.
        </p>
        <p><Path p="web/app/vite.config.ts" sym='base: "/static/app/"' />, <Path p="server/src/iki_server/web/frontend.py" sym="def page_assets(" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="router">
        <p>
          Routes are written in code in one file. The root loader reads who's signed in and their
          roles; most pages are split out and loaded when needed, and links preload on intent (<Adr
            n={[29, 176]}
          />).
        </p>
        <p><Path p={ROUTER} sym="createRootRouteWithContext" />, <Path p={ROUTER} sym='defaultPreload: "intent"' /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="layout">
        <p>
          A skip link, the sidebar, the top bar and the page, plus the ⌘K palette. The sidebar reads
          the same navigation file as the server's own pages (<Adr n="0176" />).
        </p>
        <p><Path p={`${APP}/layout.tsx`} sym="export function Layout(" />, <Path p="server/src/iki_server/web/navigation.json" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="query">
        <p>
          A <code>QueryClient</code> subclass retries a loader's read that a navigation cancelled.
          Reads stop when the document is left and resume from the back-forward cache. A 401 sends
          the person to sign in (<Adr n="0153" />).
        </p>
        <p><Path p={`${APP}/api.ts`} sym="class PageQueryClient extends QueryClient" />, <Path p={`${APP}/page-reads.ts`} sym="export const fetchPageRead" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="sdk">
        <p>
          <code>openapi-fetch</code> over a schema generated from the server's OpenAPI document. It
          sets the CSRF header on writes, or a bearer token, and turns problem responses into an
          <code>ApiError</code> (<Adr n={[27, 29]} />).
        </p>
        <p><Path p={SDK} sym="export function createIkiClient(" />, <Path p="web/packages/sdk/openapi.json" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="api">
        <p>
          The REST API with the session cookie, and one event stream per tab. Events carry ids, never
          content, and invalidate queries; a hidden tab closes its stream after five minutes (<Adr
            n="0030"
          />).
        </p>
        <p><Path p={`${APP}/events.ts`} sym="HIDDEN_GRACE_MS = 5 * 60_000" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="ui">
        <p>
          Tokens, the Inter font and three custom elements: a button, a page header and the sidebar.
          No dependencies. This site uses its tokens too (<Adr n="0191" />).
        </p>
        <p><Path p="web/packages/ui/src/button.ts" />, <Path p="web/packages/ui/src/sidebar.ts" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="science">
        <p>
          Scientific custom elements and functions, each its own entry point: the sequence and
          alignment viewers, plasmid maps, virtual gels, quantity and sequence inputs, the structure
          viewer and more (<Adr n={[87, 174, 191, 202]} />).
        </p>
        <p><Path p="web/packages/science/src/sequence-viewer.tsx" sym='customElements.define("iki-sequence-viewer"' />, <Path p="web/packages/science/package.json" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="workers">
        <p>
          iki-wasm runs in a Web Worker: the same parsers and CEL the server uses. Forms check
          plugin rules 250 ms after typing pauses, and the server checks again on save. Workers are
          created only through one Trusted Types policy (<Adr n={[90, 127]} />).
        </p>
        <p><Path p={`${APP}/workers/expressions.ts`} />, <Path p={`${APP}/rules.ts`} sym="SETTLE_MS = 250" />, <Path p={`${APP}/reading.ts`} sym='createPolicy("iki-workers"' /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="frames">
        <p>
          A plugin's component runs in an <code>iframe sandbox="allow-scripts"</code> served by its
          digest, with <code>connect-src 'none'</code>: the page fetches, and hands data in over a
          <code>MessageChannel</code> port (<Adr n={[84, 102, 117, 170]} />).
        </p>
        <p><Path p={FRAME} sym='sandbox="allow-scripts"' />, <Path p={CV} sym="component.sha256 != digest" />, <Path p="server/src/iki_server/components/bridge.js" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="still">
        <p>
          Two lint rules keep reads cancellable and stopping with the page, and a browser-test
          fixture fails any test where a press and its release land on different targets.
        </p>
        <p><Path p="eslint.config.js" sym="const QUERY_SIGNAL" />, <Path p="server/tests/click_stability.js" /></p>
      </div>
    </Diagram>

    <h3 id="frame-seq">A plugin tab, step by step</h3>
    <Sequence
      id="frame-dg"
      title="Opening /entities/PLS-…/components/iki/plasmid.plasmid_map/"
      width={900}
      actors={[
        { id: "page", label: "Page", sub: "ComponentFrame" },
        { id: "server", label: "Server" },
        { id: "frame", label: "Frame", sub: "opaque origin" },
        { id: "el", label: "Plugin element" },
      ]}
      steps={[
        { id: "list", from: "page", to: "server", label: "GET /api/v1/components: the frame's URL" },
        { id: "load", from: "page", to: "server", label: "iframe src: /plugin-components/<name>/<digest>/" },
        { id: "served", from: "server", to: "frame", label: "harden script, module (SRI), bridge; strict CSP", dashed: true },
        { id: "connect", from: "page", to: "frame", label: "iki-connect, with one MessageChannel port" },
        { id: "props", from: "frame", to: "el", label: "entity, entities, place" },
        { id: "event", from: "el", to: "frame", label: "iki-select, iki-open, iki-run" },
        { id: "check", from: "frame", to: "page", label: "over the port; the page decides" },
      ]}
    >
      <div slot="list"><p>The API gives each installed component's frame URL, digest included.</p><p><Path p="server/src/iki_server/api/components.py" sym='"frame": reverse("component_frame"' /></p></div>
      <div slot="load"><p>The frame is sandboxed with scripts only and no referrer; a frame that hasn't started in 15 seconds shows as failed.</p><p><Path p={FRAME} sym="START_TIMEOUT_MS = 15_000" /></p></div>
      <div slot="served"><p>404 unless the installed component's SHA-256 is the digest in the URL. The frame and module are cached for a year.</p><p><Path p={CV} sym='"connect-src": [CSP.NONE]' />, <Path p="server/src/iki_server/web/frame_harden.js" /></p></div>
      <div slot="connect"><p>The target origin is <code>"*"</code> because the frame's origin is opaque; the port is what stays private. If the frame loads a second document, the page closes the port and removes it.</p><p><Path p={FRAME} sym="loads.current > 1" /></p></div>
      <div slot="props"><p>The bridge accepts <code>iki-connect</code> only from its parent, then sets the element's properties. Its own comment calls it a convenience, not a guard.</p><p><Path p="server/src/iki_server/components/bridge.js" sym="const PROPERTIES" /></p></div>
      <div slot="event"><p>A component may offer its plugin's actions on its entity (<Adr n="0170" />).</p></div>
      <div slot="check"><p>The page runs an action only if the place lists it, then opens the launch page.</p><p><Path p={FRAME} sym="now.place.runs?.includes(message.action)" /></p></div>
    </Sequence>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={3} title={H.example}>
    <p>
      A scientist opens a plasmid's map tab. Django serves the shell for the path, the router matches
      the entity route, and its loader reads the record, whether the reader watches it, the types and
      the installed components in parallel. It reads the watch state before rendering because the
      watch button arriving later would move the others along:
    </p>
    <Excerpt file={ROUTER} start="^const entityRoute = createRoute\(\{" />
    <p>
      The child route for <code>components/$</code> is split out and loaded on demand. Its page
      renders a <code>ComponentFrame</code> for <code>iki/plasmid.plasmid_map</code>. Inside the
      frame the plugin's module, bundled from <Path p="plugins/plasmid/web/src/plasmid-map.js" /> and
      <code>@ikisci/science</code>'s plasmid map, draws the map from the entity the page handed it,
      with the project's primers it declared it needs:
    </p>
    <Excerpt file="plugins/plasmid/components/plasmid_map.yaml" start="^entities:" />
    <p>
      If the scientist picks one of the plugin's actions in the frame, the page checks the place
      offers it and opens the launch page.
    </p>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={4} title={H.rules}>
    <div class="rules">
      <Rule title="Reads that hold still and stop with the page" open>
        <p>Two rules in the app's ESLint config, besides jsx-a11y strict and the hooks rules:</p>
        <Excerpt file="eslint.config.js" start="^const QUERY_SIGNAL = \{" />
        <Excerpt file="eslint.config.js" start="^const POST_READ = \{" />
        <p>
          A third, <code>RAW_HTML</code>, bans <code>dangerouslySetInnerHTML</code>, which Trusted
          Types would refuse anyway.
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="Pages that hold still under a press">
        <p>
          Loaders read everything that decides a toolbar before the first render. Tab rows draw only
          when settled, with placeholders holding their place; overview cards are laid out hidden
          until each reports settled or a time budget runs out, and a late card draws into a fixed
          reserve. The grid keeps its rows while a new filter loads (<Path
            p={`${APP}/settling.tsx`}
            sym="export function useSettled("
          />, <Path p={`${APP}/tab-strip.tsx`} />).
        </p>
        <p>
          Buttons that can't be pressed set <code>aria-disabled</code> or <code>aria-busy</code> and
          swallow the press, rather than using the native <code>disabled</code> attribute (<Path
            p="web/packages/ui/src/button.ts"
            sym="if (unavailable) event.preventDefault();"
          />). <Inferred why="No comment or ADR says why.">That keeps them focusable and in place.</Inferred>
          The app makes no optimistic updates.
        </p>
        <p>
          The browser tests install a script in every page and frame that records each press and
          release and every layout shift; a test fails when a press and its release land on different
          targets (<Path p="server/tests/conftest.py" sym="def _watch_browser_click_stability(" />, <Path
            p="server/tests/click_stability.py"
          />).
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="The SDK, generated and checked">
        <p>
          <code>make client</code> writes the OpenAPI document from the server, then the TypeScript
          schema from it. Two checks catch drift: a server test compares the committed document with
          the live schema, and <code>make check-web</code> regenerates the TypeScript and diffs it (<Path
            p="server/tests/test_web_app.py"
            sym="def test_the_published_openapi_document_is_current("
          />, <Path p="scripts/check-client.sh" />). The <a href="/routes/">route list</a> on this site
          is read from the same document.
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="Packages">
        <ul>
          <li><Path p="web/app" label="@ikisci/app" />: the React app, private</li>
          <li><Path p="web/packages/sdk" label="@ikisci/sdk" />: the generated client</li>
          <li><Path p="web/packages/ui" label="@ikisci/ui" />: tokens and basic elements, published</li>
          <li><Path p="web/packages/science" label="@ikisci/science" />: scientific elements and functions, published</li>
          <li><Path p="web/packages/component" label="@ikisci/component" />: types and helpers for plugin authors' components</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Plugin components with source under <code>web/</code> are bundled into one self-contained
          module each, and <code>pnpm test</code> fails on a stale bundle (<Adr n="0191" />, <Path
            p="scripts/bundle-plugin-components.mjs"
          />).
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="Every routed page is served">
        <p>
          A test reads the route tree and checks that every page the app routes answers 200 from
          Django, and another that each sidebar item is a page (<Path
            p="server/tests/test_web_app.py"
            sym="def test_every_page_the_app_routes_loads_it("
          />).
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="The page's content security policy">
        <p>
          Trusted Types are required for scripts, with exactly one policy, <code>iki-workers</code>,
          which allows only Iki's own worker scripts. Worker scripts get a policy of their own that
          allows WebAssembly (<Path p="server/src/iki_server/settings.py" sym='"trusted-types": ["iki-workers"]' />, <Path
            p="server/src/iki_server/web/static_headers.py"
            sym="WORKER_CSP = ("
          />).
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="Where the ADRs and the code differ">
        <ul>
          <li>
            <Adr n="0029" /> says the policy allows no Trusted Types policies; the code has one, for
            workers. Comments in <Path p={`${APP}/uploads.ts`} /> and <Path p="web/app/README.md" /> still
            say workers aren't allowed.
          </li>
          <li>
            <Adr n="0012" /> says a component fetches its own data with the viewer's permissions. Under
            <Adr n="0084" /> its frame can't connect anywhere; the page fetches for it.
          </li>
          <li>
            <Adr n="0029" /> describes the app as home and project pages; it now also routes records,
            runs, storage, files and admin compute pages (<Adr n="0176" />).
          </li>
          <li>
            <code>@ikisci/component</code>'s place type has no <code>runs</code>, though <Adr
              n="0170"
            />, the bridge and the app support offering actions.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </Rule>
    </div>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={5} title={H.ref}>
    <div class="refs">
      <h3>Where</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><Path p={ROUTER} />: every route and loader</li>
        <li><Path p={`${APP}/api.ts`} />: the client and query defaults</li>
        <li><Path p={FRAME} />: plugin frames on the page</li>
        <li><Path p="server/src/iki_server/components" />: serving frames, and the bridge</li>
        <li><Path p="server/src/iki_server/web" />: the page shell, static files and frames</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Decisions</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><Adr n="0012" title /></li>
        <li><Adr n="0029" title /></li>
        <li><Adr n="0030" title /></li>
        <li><Adr n="0084" title /></li>
        <li><Adr n="0102" title /></li>
        <li><Adr n="0103" title /></li>
        <li><Adr n="0170" title /></li>
        <li><Adr n="0176" title /></li>
        <li><Adr n="0191" title /></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </Layer>
</Layout>
